Done. Here's what I built:

`/skill search [query]` — a new subcommand that discovers yoyo skills on GitHub.

### What it does:
1. Checks if gh CLI is available (clear error message if not)
2. Searches GitHub for repos with the yoyo-skill topic first
3. Falls back to text search for "yoyo-skill" if no topic-based results
4. Displays results in a formatted table: repo name, description, last updated date
5. Shows install hint so users can immediately gh:owner/repo the skill

### Changes:
• `src/commands_skill.rs` — Added `"search" to SKILL_SUBCOMMANDS, wired into handle_skill(), implemented handle_skill_search()` with topic-based and text fallback search via `gh search repos --json`, plus a minimal JSON parser (avoids serde_json dependency). 8 new tests covering JSON parsing, escape handling, null values, empty inputs, and routing.
• `src/help.rs` — Updated all 5 locations referencing skill commands to include search
• `README.md` — Updated skills system description to mention search
• `docs/src/configuration/skills.md` — Added "Searching for skills" section with usage examples

### Design decisions:
• Uses `--json fullName,description,updatedAt` for structured output instead of parsing tab-separated text — more reliable
• Hand-rolled JSON parser instead of adding serde_json — keeps dependencies minimal, only needs 3 string fields
• Safe string truncation with `is_char_boundary()` for repo names (follows project safety rules)
• `yoyo-skill` topic convention enables decentralized discovery without a central registry

